WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.334
- There was a chance we were
gonna see

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.711
all three of y'all on a team?

00:00:02.711 --> 00:00:04.754
- Me, Bron and D

00:00:04.754 --> 00:00:06.715
almost had a chance one time,

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:09.676
but we didn't know who was gonna
wear No. 3.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.137
- [Announcer:] Oh!
- [Second announcer:]
Oh, Paul again

00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:15.223
pulls off his magic.
- [Laughing]

00:00:15.223 --> 00:00:18.768
- True or false, and why:
The Rockets should have beaten

00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:20.687
the Warriors in the playoffs.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.105
- You know, that was one of
the toughest things

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:23.481
I think I dealt with.

00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:26.192
- [Announcer:] Ball. Got around
the screen this time.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.653
- What if that trade was able

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:30.321
to happen with the Lakers?
- I knew that was coming.

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:33.783
It's even crazier
to think about it now,

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:37.203
losing Kobe and David Stern.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.122
Man, it would've—
it've been special.

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:44.544
♪♪♪

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.046
Hey, what's up?
I'm Chris Paul—

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:49.174
point guard for
the Oklahoma City Thunder.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:53.011
Wake Forest alumnus,
North Carolina boy.

00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:55.764
Here about to answer
a few questions about myself,

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:58.224
the season, everything else
that's going on in life.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.726
So, yep, I'm about to
"Take It There"

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.394
with Taylor Rooks.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.396
- [Announcer:] Oh! Can you
make it two in a row?

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.316
He can—as he splashes home!

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:07.275
- [Taylor Rooks:]
OK, so first off,

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:09.069
thank you for spending
your off time here

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:12.072
on the show, bowling, Chris.
- Yeah, because my off days,

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.239
I don't like to be around him.

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.241
- [Taylor, chuckling:]
But you're stuck with him today?

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:16.576
- For right now.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.078
- Is he, is he gonna do this
the whole time?

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:20.080
- Wait, hold on. Tell her why
you don't like being around me.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.082
I beat him in everything we do.
Competing—it doesn't matter.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:24.042
[Crowd cheering]

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.711
- [Announcer:]
Shai Gilgeous-Alexander!

00:01:28.463 --> 00:01:32.300
- [Second announcer:]
SGA lines it up. Right down
the pipe from downtown.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:36.471
[Cheering, shouting]

00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:38.640
- Well, he's supposed to be,
like, the best bowler.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.725
Are you the best bowler
in the NBA?

00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:42.268
- I don't know.
I feel like I'm up there.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:44.395
- All right, well, now
it's your turn to show us.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:46.773
You're up first.
- Aw, man.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:49.067
- Let's see what he's
talking about, Shai.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.611
- Shai, what we gonna do?
We bowling for push-ups?

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.946
- Nah.
- [Taylor:] So what?

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:55.323
- [Chris Paul:]
What are we bowling for then?

00:01:55.323 --> 00:01:57.325
Push-ups.

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.868
♪♪♪- Let's go ♪♪♪

00:01:58.868 --> 00:01:59.786
- Here we go, C.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:00.870
♪♪♪- Let's go ♪♪♪

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.455
-Here we go.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:04.290
♪♪♪- Let's go ♪♪♪

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.377
- Oh, no, she didn't.

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:11.673
- Oh! Boom. Boom, boom,
boom, boom, boom.

00:02:11.673 --> 00:02:13.883
That's how you do it.
Crunch time.

00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:16.386
I'm a clutch player.
I'm a clutch player.

00:02:16.386 --> 00:02:17.512
How old are you, Shai?

00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:19.013
- Twenty-one.
I ain't got gray hair.

00:02:19.013 --> 00:02:20.723
- They make you feel old,
don't they, Chris?

00:02:20.723 --> 00:02:23.268
- We don't make him
feel nothing.
He's naturally just old.

00:02:23.268 --> 00:02:25.145
- [Chris:]
Till he steps on the court.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:28.231
He be so happy on my team now
and he ain't gotta guard me.

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:31.860
- [Laughing] No!

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.695
- Strike club? OK—
- Listen, I promise—

00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:35.363
- Yeah, strike club. Have you
ever got a strike?

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:36.990
- If he would've got a strike
right there,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.533
this whole interview thing
was over.

00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:39.826
I was going home.
- [Laughing]

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:40.994
♪♪♪

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.747
- So when we were bowling, Shai
jokingly said that you're old.

00:02:44.747 --> 00:02:46.541
- Yep.
- Do you feel old?

00:02:46.541 --> 00:02:48.668
- By no means. By no means.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.837
- What is it like being
a leader in the NBA?

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.131
Cuz, it's funny, you know,
whenever I do these interviews,

00:02:53.131 --> 00:02:55.049
I always ask different guys
about who I'm interviewing

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:56.885
to get stories, get questions,

00:02:56.885 --> 00:02:59.220
and people absolutely
see you as a leader.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.973
You're a player people
come to for advice,

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.516
when they just have questions.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:05.351
Does a lot of weight
come with that?

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.688
- It's a lot of weight.
It's a lot of responsibility.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:11.316
But I think
the coolest thing for me

00:03:11.316 --> 00:03:13.193
is that, you know, obviously,

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.486
people are always
looking to me for advice

00:03:15.486 --> 00:03:16.988
or how can I help them.

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:19.365
- At this point in your career,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:23.203
what's more important:
money or a championship?

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.538
- I mean, obviously I want to
win a championship,

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.707
but am I gonna...
you know what I mean?

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.334
- Mmhmm.
- Like, are you here

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.211
doing this for free?
- I am not.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:33.046
- No. Exactly.
You know what I'm saying?
- [Taylor:] Yeah.

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:35.215
- So, like, I got a family
I gotta take care of.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.550
Now, when I compete
- Yeah.
- like, I'm competing.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.553
I always want to win.
I'm unbelievably competitive.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:46.059
But I got a lot of great stuff
that goes on in my life.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.478
I've got two beautiful kids,
an amazing wife,

00:03:48.478 --> 00:03:50.146
and I got a whole family.

00:03:50.146 --> 00:03:52.315
I don't go to bed,
like, with a picture

00:03:52.315 --> 00:03:53.858
of the trophy, like,

00:03:53.858 --> 00:03:56.236
"Ooh, I gotta have it.
I gotta have it."

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.404
No, not on duty.
- Yeah. OK.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.572
- Yeah.
- No, that makes sense.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.574
There's things bigger than
just winning that championship.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:04.244
- But that doesn't mean
I don't want to win it

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:06.120
and that I'm not going
to strive to win it.
- Mmhmm.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.792
- But is that my, like,
ultimate goal in life?

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.418
Absolutely not.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.920
- What is your ultimate goal
in life?

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.798
- I got a lasting imprint
that I not only want

00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:21.886
to try to, you know,
make on others, but my kids.

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:23.429
- No, I feel that.
- So, yeah,

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.891
the NBA championship—
kiss all of my ass.

00:04:26.891 --> 00:04:30.436
Like, Little Chris and Camryn
is my priority.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.230
- That's great. OK.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:34.399
So if you could be commissioner
of the NBA for one day—

00:04:34.399 --> 00:04:36.776
- One day.
- You got one day.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.737
You can change one
on-the-court rule.

00:04:39.737 --> 00:04:44.450
- That's tough. Man.
Uh...shoot.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.452
Man, I'd probably
lower the goals

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.037
at least for one quarter.

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:49.664
[Taylor scoffing]
Listen. Listen.

00:04:49.664 --> 00:04:51.165
I got all types of dunks
I'd be doing.

00:04:51.165 --> 00:04:52.458
- [Taylor:]
What are you trying to do?

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:53.751
- Lower the goal
for one quarter.

00:04:53.751 --> 00:04:55.878
- [Laughing]
- Um, and—

00:04:55.878 --> 00:04:58.298
- From what—10 to what?
Like, how low are we going?

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.758
- I mean, I might just need
like nine and a half.

00:05:00.758 --> 00:05:02.010
The game is the game.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.386
- Was that a "The Wire"
reference?

00:05:03.386 --> 00:05:04.929
- Huh?
- "The game is the game."

00:05:04.929 --> 00:05:06.472
- Have you seen "The Wire"?
- Have I seen "The Wire"?

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.057
- OK, I just needed
to make sure.

00:05:08.057 --> 00:05:10.059
- My alias on the road
used to be Avon Barksdale.

00:05:10.059 --> 00:05:11.477
- No way.
- [Chris:] Yeah, come on.
Don't do that.

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.313
- Should've gone, like,
maybe Marlo.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.732
- No, no—Avon.
- Maybe a little Stringer Bell.

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:18.318
- Not Stringer Bell—
it was Avon Barksdale.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:22.989
- OK, so as a TV guy,
if you could pick one TV world

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.490
and you're one
fictional character

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.035
in this TV world,
what are you picking?

00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:28.995
- The character that I really,

00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:33.499
really, like, got attached to
was Jax Teller.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.044
Started watching
"Sons of Anarchy," and listen,

00:05:36.044 --> 00:05:37.920
that right there goes, like,
with "The Wire."

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.381
That's one of the best shows—
- No!

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:42.717
- Watch it. Just watch it.
Cuz, I mean—

00:05:42.717 --> 00:05:44.510
- I don't know if bikers
are for me.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.346
- I didn't think it was
for me either.
- [Taylor:] Yeah.

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:49.015
- But at the end of the day,
once you start watching a show,

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.017
it's about all the stories
that's being told.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.811
That's what gets you attached
to the show is the characters.

00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:56.647
- Well, on every TV show,
every main character,

00:05:56.647 --> 00:05:58.524
they have a flaw.
What's your flaw?

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.401
- That's probably a better
question for my wife.

00:06:00.401 --> 00:06:02.028
- [Laughing]
- But, I mean,

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:04.697
I got a lot of them.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:09.202
I'm probably not very patient,
anxious a lot of times.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:11.579
I'm sure some people would
probably say I'm pushy or bossy

00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:13.039
and all the different
type stuff,

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:16.292
so, I mean, I could
run down a whole list.

00:06:16.292 --> 00:06:18.878
♪♪♪
- When I was researching
for this interview,

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:21.005
one thing that comes up
is these articles

00:06:21.005 --> 00:06:22.840
that talk about you
being a bad teammate.

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:24.300
- Mmm.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:27.637
- Which—I have never heard
a player personally say,

00:06:27.637 --> 00:06:29.013
"Chris is a bad teammate."

00:06:29.013 --> 00:06:30.932
I've never heard anything
like that before.

00:06:30.932 --> 00:06:33.393
Why do you think that
narrative exists about you?

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:37.730
- [Chris:]
Some of the people say it that
I may have been teammates with.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:41.442
We did get into it,
or we did have a falling out

00:06:41.442 --> 00:06:44.028
or altercation,
and that's that.

00:06:44.028 --> 00:06:46.197
- Have you ever wanted
to resolve it with them?

00:06:46.197 --> 00:06:48.032
- I think so.
If that was the case,

00:06:48.032 --> 00:06:50.576
I would more so, like,
want to know what the issue is.

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:53.746
I mean, some of them I sort of
know what the issue is,

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:56.124
but I think I try to control
what I can control.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:59.001
You know, some of my teammates
like David West,

00:06:59.001 --> 00:07:03.840
who I played with in New Orleans
who is, like, my guy forever.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.758
Like, we still talk.
- [Taylor:] Mmhmm.
- You know what I mean?

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:09.053
And I played
with the Clippers.

00:07:09.053 --> 00:07:12.390
I still talk to DJ
about every day.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:15.768
Talk to JJ Redick all the time.
Just about all the guys

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:17.770
that I played with there,
you know what I mean?

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.605
Still talk to Tuck
and all these guys,

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:22.108
Eric Gordon
and all these guys, so.

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:25.570
- So this idea that you
just, like, dislike the Rockets

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.738
and don't ever want to talk
to them again is false?

00:07:27.738 --> 00:07:29.323
- When the stuff happened
with the Rockets,

00:07:29.323 --> 00:07:32.952
I just wasn't happy about
how it went down.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.163
As far as—
I know it's a business.

00:07:35.163 --> 00:07:38.124
You got to do what you got
to do, but we're adults.

00:07:38.124 --> 00:07:40.501
We can communicate.
I just had a conversation

00:07:40.501 --> 00:07:43.880
with him a few days before that
and he was like,

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.632
"We ain't gonna trade you
to the, uh, Oklahoma."

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.885
He asked me,
"Do you wanna go there?"

00:07:48.885 --> 00:07:51.053
I said, "No, not at this point
in my career."

00:07:51.053 --> 00:07:52.555
He said, "All right,
I won't trade you there

00:07:52.555 --> 00:07:55.725
because you chose
to come to us from L.A."

00:07:55.725 --> 00:07:57.810
That was that. But I mean,
they don't owe me nothing.
- [Taylor:] Yeah.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.771
- So thankfully everything
happens for a reason.

00:08:00.771 --> 00:08:06.611
♪♪♪

00:08:06.611 --> 00:08:09.155
- Oh, shit.
- I didn't even see it.

00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:10.698
What happened?
- Dang!

00:08:10.698 --> 00:08:12.325
- [Chris:] I didn't even
seen it. What happened?

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:14.076
You know I quit school, right?

00:08:14.076 --> 00:08:16.078
Because of recess.
I don't play.

00:08:16.078 --> 00:08:18.372
[Laughing]
- [Taylor:] This is it.
I can feel it.

00:08:18.372 --> 00:08:20.082
[Shai Gilgeous-Alexander
clearing throat]
- [Chris:] Oh, this guy—

00:08:20.082 --> 00:08:21.501
- That's crazy.
- See?

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:22.877
That's what he do
in shooting games too.

00:08:22.877 --> 00:08:24.879
- [Taylor:] But, see,
I can eliminate distraction.

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:27.131
- [Shai:] Oh, just like you did.
- [Taylor:] Yep. I didn't go.

00:08:29.217 --> 00:08:31.344
- Oh, oh, no, she didn't.

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:33.471
- Oh!
- [Shai:] Oh,
y'all are taking this

00:08:33.471 --> 00:08:34.972
a little too serious now.
- [Taylor:] Dang!

00:08:34.972 --> 00:08:36.432
- Y'all lucky I didn't
warm up too.

00:08:36.432 --> 00:08:37.683
- [Chris:] Man, shut up.

00:08:39.644 --> 00:08:41.187
- Damn.
- No, he ain't got it.

00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:43.481
He ain't got it.
- [Shai:] Ah!

00:08:43.481 --> 00:08:44.815
Let's go back
to playing basketball.

00:08:44.815 --> 00:08:48.152
This ain't it right now.
[Laughing]

00:08:48.152 --> 00:08:50.905
- OK, if you could build
the ultimate point guard—

00:08:50.905 --> 00:08:52.490
OK, you have to take
attributes

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:53.783
from different point guards

00:08:53.783 --> 00:08:55.576
to build that great one.

00:08:55.576 --> 00:08:57.203
- Hmm.
- Build it.

00:08:57.203 --> 00:09:00.206
- You know, I probably want
D-Rose's explosiveness.

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:01.874
And then you got
the different arms.

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:04.126
So, like, want one hand
probably, like,

00:09:04.126 --> 00:09:06.045
Kyrie's finishes and all that.

00:09:06.045 --> 00:09:09.215
And then on the other hand,
Shai nice with the finishes.

00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:12.426
Like, Steve Nash was
a really good shooter.

00:09:12.426 --> 00:09:14.053
Russ—a great rebounder.

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:16.722
You know, Bron is always
good at passing

00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:18.307
and all that different
type stuff.

00:09:18.307 --> 00:09:21.686
But I know, like, my basketball
IQ and awareness,

00:09:21.686 --> 00:09:23.688
like, nobody
watches more basketball

00:09:23.688 --> 00:09:25.022
than me,
you know what I mean?

00:09:25.022 --> 00:09:27.400
So probably like D-Will

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:30.069
or Baron Davis', like, build.

00:09:30.069 --> 00:09:32.613
Shooting also might be
somebody like Gilbert Arenas.

00:09:32.613 --> 00:09:34.282
Like, Gil—see,
that's what I'm saying.

00:09:34.282 --> 00:09:36.242
Like, that's why I get mad
when I'm talking to Shai

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:38.119
and guys like that,
cuz they don't be realizing

00:09:38.119 --> 00:09:40.413
how nice people like Gil was.
- [Taylor:] Right.

00:09:40.413 --> 00:09:42.123
- [Chris:] I'm constantly
on YouTube with Shai

00:09:42.123 --> 00:09:44.166
and all of them showing them,
like,

00:09:44.166 --> 00:09:45.793
"This was Gil right here."

00:09:45.793 --> 00:09:46.961
- Yeah.
- You know what I mean?

00:09:46.961 --> 00:09:50.381
And that's why they know that
I'm always harping on defense.

00:09:50.381 --> 00:09:52.383
